64 973 64 \nQ 1203 64 1331 192 \nQ 1459 320 1459 557 \nQ 1459 845 1101 1293 \nQ 698 1798 698 2131 \nQ 698 2451 909 2636 \nQ 1120 2822 1472 2822 \nQ 1600 2822 1830 2758 \nQ 1971 2714 2061 2714 \nQ 2189 2714 2253 2829 \nL 2342 2829 \nz\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"></path></defs><use xlink:href=\"#STIXGeneral-Italic-73\" transform=\"translate(0 0.796875)\"></use></g></g><g id=\"text_6\"><!-- $\\mathit{t}$ --><g transform=\"translate(16.711364 16.011562) scale(0.13 -0.13)\"><defs><path id=\"STIXGeneral-Italic-74\" d=\"M 1894 2739 \nL 1862 2534 \nL 1325 2534 \nL 768 435 \nQ 755 384 755 346 \nQ 755 243 851 243 \nQ 928 243 1030 342 \nQ 1133 442 1370 749 \nL 1453 704 \nQ 1158 256 969 93 \nQ 781 -70 538 -70 \nQ 243 -70 243 166 \nQ 243 230 346 640 \nL 845 2534 \nL 365 2534 \nL 358 2573 \nQ 358 2688 570 2733 \nQ 730 2771 992 2979 \nQ 1254 3187 1421 3437 \nQ 1459 3494 1510 3494 \nQ 1568 3494 1568 3443 \nQ 1568 3411 1562 3398 \nL 1382 2739 \nL 1894 2739 \nz\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"></path></defs><use xlink:href=\"#STIXGeneral-Italic-74\" transform=\"translate(0 0.40625)\"></use></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pa3fb9f1779\"><rect x=\"7.2\" y=\"13.078804\" width=\"209.25\" height=\"207.9\"></rect></clipPath></defs></svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for diagram of 3 lines\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>Clockwise from top left, the 3 lines are labeled t, r, and s.</li><li>Line t intersects both line r and line s.</li><li>At the intersection of line t and line r, 1 angle is labeled clockwise from top left as follows:<br><ul><li>Bottom right: 24°</li></ul></li><li>At the intersection of line t and line s, 1 angle is labeled clockwise from top left as follows:<br><ul><li>Top left: x°</li></ul></li><li>Note: Figure not drawn to scale.</li></ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the figure, line <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> intersects lines <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math>. Which additional piece of information is sufficient to prove that lines <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math> are parallel?</p>", "keys": ["5230d681-92dd-4d64-b3d8-4f029ab068a5"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "d12db8e3-2f84-47d0-bc78-cbe6ac817fc4", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"x less than 24\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>24</mn></math></p>"}, {"id": "5230d681-92dd-4d64-b3d8-4f029ab068a5", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"x equals 24\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "c37e6946-c0ed-4fff-9e1e-439e96236493", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"x greater than 24\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>24</mn></math></p>"}, {"id": "1ff8ae42-c1a7-4554-82fd-dd821196f061", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"x minus 24 equals 360\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>360</mn></math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. In the figure shown, transversal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> intersects&nbsp;lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math>. Two lines intersected by a transversal are parallel if and only if a pair of alternate interior angles have equal measure. The angle marked <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"24 degree\"><mn>24</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and the angle marked <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x degree\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> form a pair of alternate interior angles. Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals 24\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math> is sufficient to prove that lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math> are parallel.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>", "externalid": "3f1bac86-dd93-4b6b-960c-c29978b05446", "correct_answer": ["B"]}